[491.406375, "o", "According to adjacency_rules.py:\r\n- Geothermal gives +2 based on FEATURE check\r\n- Districts give +0.5 per 2 based on placement check\r\n\r\nThe question is: when City Center is on Geothermal, does it count for BOTH?\r\n\r\nLooking at count_rule_sources in adjacency_rules.py:\r\n- It checks for features first (geothermal, reef, etc.)\r\n- Then checks for districts in placements\r\n- The 'matched = True; break' logic prevents double-counting the SAME neighbor\r\n\r\nSo if (21,13) has Geothermal AND is City Center:\r\n- It matches Geothermal first -> +2\r\n"]
[491.406409, "o", "- The 'break' prevents it from also counting as a district\r\n\r\nThis means Campus adjacency is:\r\n- Geothermal (21,13): +2 (City Center doesn't also count)\r\n- Reef (20,14): +2\r\n- Mountain (21,15): +1\r\n- 2 Jungles: floor(2/2) = +1\r\n- 1 District (Commercial Hub only): floor(1/2) = +0\r\n"]
[491.406592, "o", "- Total: 6\r\n\r\nBut wait - let me check if this is the intended behavior...\r\nActually, looking more carefully at the code, the 'break' is per-rule, not per-neighbor\r\nSo each neighbor is only counted once PER RULE, but can count for different rules\r\n"]
